   "summary": "Practice day \u2014 testing the range levels on purpose. Yes, too many trades, but I was testing levels. Took a call that won, then jumped in at the right level for the put dump, but didn't realise how much cash I'd used, so I had to buy a really far out-of-the-money put. It still paid. I was okay with how it went \u2014 still practicing.",
   "right": "Two real reads made +$330: the 6:51 C650 caught the 636 \u2192 643 pop (+$88, added into a winner), and the 7:07 P621 \u00d72 at 0.37 caught the dump after the failed push at 643 \u2014 held 19 min with a raised stop, sold 1.58 (+$242). Every stop $0.15 or tighter, no chasing. Ended +$199.",
   "fix": "Testing the $634\u2013638 chop cost \u2212$128 over 12 tries and broke the \u2212$75 stop by 6:49 (\u2212$85); 7 entries in each of the first two 20-min candles. Practice rule: 1 contract, 2 tries, then wait \u2014 the tests cost ~$30 and the cash is still there for the real setup.",
